### Key Distinction from Previous Evaluation

An existing evaluation (`evaluation/generalization_eval_summary.json`) claimed PASS for all items, but that evaluation relied on **execution-based verification** (testing on different model variants and datasets). Under the read-only evaluation rules where execution is not allowed, those empirical verifications cannot be used as evidence. The documentation alone does not provide explicit justification for generalization claims - it actually transparently acknowledges these as limitations.
